really cool charity hockey game this  weekend will go a long way to help  veterans with medical sponsorships the  coast to coast foundation and vegas  veterans hockey foundation are hosting  the game at city national arena it's  part of the foundation's ride for the  fallen a 4 000 mile cross-country  journey from la to arlington national  cemetery several vets former nhl and  european players and our own john  langler will participate each player  will wear a jersey with the name of a  military member who made the ultimate  sacrifice something that makes this game  that much more special  there's nothing more more great than you  know watching your brothers and sisters  out on the ice  and having the opportunity to wear a  jersey that represents each one of those  fallen heroes and when that name goes on  you're on your back and you you know  that you're representing that fallen  soldier  it's meaningful and it's impactful  coast to coast is a non-profit  organization that provides medical  sponsorships for veterans of the special  ops community puck drop for the game is  1 pm tomorrow tickets are 10 kids 13  under are free all proceeds go to the  vets
 

